A||||18||Loki||Anyone fill bankruptcy?||||1||
Z||000000||Loki||08-29-2001||08:00 PM||||  This is one option im looking at to get my happy ass outta debt. Im 25 years old and over 35k in debt. Im having a very hard time making my payments. If anyone has filled please enlighten me on what needs to be done? Pros and Cons and all that good stuff. Also im not worried about my credit rating right now in life.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/loki-mg/loki_sig.jpg">  <BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>http://members.home.net/loki-mg||||reg||1
Z||000001||starfighter007@msn.com||08-29-2001||08:07 PM||||no sorry I have been lucky I guess sorry to hear.but If it were me I would be worried at any point in life about a bad credit raing like bankruptcy I think that can haunt you your whole life I dont buy that your record is clear after seven years I maybe wrong though. but I wish you well||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||08-29-2001||08:43 PM||||I did it when I got a divorce. Not that big a deal. Varies between states. You have to go thru a lawyer and list all your debts. Then if anybody you owe wants to contest it they go to the court. Nobody usually does, they just write it off. Anything you want to keep (ie=car) you can just sign a waiver that lets you continue payments just like you did before. The only thing anyone came to get back was an almost new big screen tv. Credit card places dont even bother, I owed AMEX like $3000 and had just bought a new high line camcorder and I kept it too. Dont let anyone tell you it totally ruins your credit, after a few years, I bought a Limo Service with 4 Limos, had 3 new credit cards with $10,000 limits, bought a Mercedes SL, a JetBoat, and an airplane. I know in Texas a bankruptcy cant take house or property. Most states cant touch "tools of your trade" wont touch personal belongings like clothes except for maybe furs and jewelry. In ohio, after 8 years it disappears from your credit record.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Urchin||08-29-2001||08:47 PM||||I've never filed but just to let you know that you aren't alone.  I've wracked up about $15,000 in personal loans and a $13,000 car loan.  I'm 24 and ya, it's tough to be in that much debt when you are only this far into your independant stage of life.  If you haven't already..consolodate them.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/side_cut_sig_4.jpg">  <BR>If you can read this, I'm parked.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Loki||08-29-2001||09:08 PM||||I looked into consolidating my debt, but what they wanted me to pay and what I was already paying was hardly ANY difference... I may talk with a lawyer next week and see what they have to say. I just need to get this crap behind me so I can restart my life and worry about my son. Thanx for the info, it opened my eyes a bit more about it....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||My7Fieros||08-29-2001||09:17 PM||||I never have, but I know lots of people who have..and it IS a big deal. Like previously stated, it varies from state to state, but usually at bare minimun it stays on your credit report for 7 or 8 years (remember, minimum)...thats a ****ing long ass time. They are two different kinds of b.r..... chapter 7 and chapter 13 (ironic lucky and unlucky numbers huh)....you may want to look into the differences in the two and determine which is right for you (should you decide to do it).<BR>There was a thing on the news the other night about some states "doing away" of sorts, with bankrupcy....seems so many people do it because they get in over their heads, then use it for an easy "bail out".<BR>Anyway, think hard about it before you do, and should you file, check into the different ones....... <FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>7</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Old Lar||08-29-2001||09:47 PM||||Remember you cannot file for bankrupcy a second time for (8)? years.  You'll get accepted for many high interest credit cards so you can rack up more debt.  Then you are really stuck.  Forget about getting bank loans (maybe finance companies at 23% or more interest), no house you can buy.<P>Think about it long and hard.  You'll be pushing 40 by the time your credit is straightened out.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Loki||08-29-2001||09:54 PM||||As far as other credit cards..I dont care about em....I hurt myself bad by using them like I did. As for a house. I already have one and 16 acres in the country..So im not worried about that.||||reg||1
Z||000008||rogergarrison||08-29-2001||10:12 PM||||I use my credit cards to buy big ticket items like a cmtr, tires, etc so I can keep track of what im spending-then pay it off when I get the bill just saves hauling lots of cash around. Its amazing how much farther your money goes when you dont make payments to anyone. I dont know about your state Lar, but I bought my $75,000 plane and $200,000 house with bank loans. <p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 08-29-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||maryjane||08-29-2001||11:13 PM||||anyone know if backtaxes (federal) are covered by filing bankruptcy? I would think not, but always wondered about that.||||reg||1
Z||000010||rogergarrison||08-29-2001||11:34 PM||||nope.......government always gets theres<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cheever3000||08-30-2001||12:28 AM||||RG is right.  Not such a big deal.  But with mine, one of the creditors I did <B>not</B> wish to include decided to be part of it too.  My lawyer didn't understand why they would want to do that, since I couldn't do it again for another 7 to 10 years (depending on who you talk to), they had nothing to lose by keeping me as a customer, but it was their perogative.  <P>Also, when the discharge date comes (the day it becomes official and you sit in front of a judge and say yes I understand what I'm doing), any of your creditors may appear to argue their right to the money you owe them, or to at least get their products back.  My lawyer told me don't worry even if they do show up, but none of them did. <P>As of my discharge date in January '89, the word was it would be on your credit record for 7 years.  Soon after, it became 10 years.  It could be more now, for all I know.  The only downsides to me were that I couldn't buy a house all that time (yes I tried), and I knew that I HAD to be more careful because it would mean big trouble if I got in over my head again.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000012||DecadenceR||08-30-2001||12:34 AM||||Back taxes, student loans, or any other government funded money are not covered in bankruptcy. <BR>I read a few things abotu it recently.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Monkeyman||08-30-2001||06:23 AM||||I haven't filed yet, but will in the near future.  My best friends bankruptcy will be final soon and my wifes bankruptcy was final just before we got married.  No problems anywhere.  My wife and I bought a house about a year ago and my wife has a 3 year old car she bought new.  I wouldn't worry too much about your credit w/ bankruptcy.  If you're considering bankruptcy, your credit is already shot to hell.  I don't care about the credit cards, etc.  I'm just tired of knowing that I'll never get ahead because of all the bills I owe.  I think you'll find that soon after your bankruptcy is finalized, you'll get all kinds of offers for loans, etc.  Creditors know that you can't file again for 7 years.  I wouldn't take bankruptcy lightly, but don't shy away from it thinking that it will ruin your life.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000014||LarryB||08-30-2001||11:46 AM||||A bankruptcy report will in reality show up on your credit history until the reporting bureau removes it.  In practice they do not automatically remove the report when the legally mandated interval has expired, so you will need to obtain copies of your credit report from each of the reporting agencies and contact them to make sure the entry is removed. <P>My guess behing Cheever3000's problem with the vendor was that they figured if they got in while you still had assets to divide they would recover at least some of their money, otherwise they felt they risked losing it all. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Cheever3000||08-30-2001||12:06 PM||||One more thing: when you fill out applications for various things that ask if you've filed for bankruptcy in the last 10 years, you must say "yes", but after that time you are not required to mention it to anybody, period.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||thomas_l||08-30-2001||01:01 PM||||7 years for Ch 13 and 10 years for Ch 7. Some people don't have too many issues. I did a Ch 7 in 88 and had some weasels keep accounts "open" and continue to report them as I9 on the credit report. Basically making a bad thing look REALLY bad. Also any judgements are slow to move off your record. If you do a bankruptcy, plan on making your credit file a part time occupation, not just a house-buying, fraud prevention excercise. I will work 4 jobs and die paying before I even think about it again. Yah, some people say phooey I'll just use cash, but nowadays you can't do sh1t without some use of credit somewhere. Or you spend more cash just to avoid it.||||reg||1
Z||000017||ferg||08-30-2001||01:41 PM||||Loki- you didn't mention what type of debt it was. If it's personal loans- could you try and sell the items? If you have credit card debts, call the credit card companies, and see if they will wave the interest. If you explain that you are having a hard time making the payments and are considering bankruptcy they might give up or lower the interest so they can get their money back. <P>To the credit card companies- if you file bankruptcy then they can't collect anything, but if they wave the interest or lower it a bunch, they stand a much better chance of getting their money back.<P>On a side note- $35k isn't all that bad. You can get yourself out this with some time. Personally, I wouldn't want to file unless it was the last option available. You may clear your debt, but it may be harder to move forward in your life (i.e. buy a house)||||reg||1
Z||000018||Loki||08-30-2001||05:03 PM||||Its mainly CC debt with 2 loans.  Im sure I could do it, but with evewryhting going on in lfe right now (I havnt seen my son in 5 months) Its just taking its toll on me mentally and physically dealing with it all..I just want it behind me so I can atleast try and have a life agian...||||reg||1
